WEBVTT

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:06.420
In the midst of investigating
nightmares occurring in Sinnoh,

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.780
Satoshi and Go
are in pursuit of Darkrai.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.990
Meanwhile, Koharu and Eevee
were traveling in Sinnoh...

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:16.080
...and met Hikari,
a girl headed for a Contest.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.470
At a forest they wandered into,
the two of them found...

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.250
Cresselia...

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:05.960
Cresselia. Crescent Moon Pokémon.
Psychic type.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:08.350
It is referred to as
the crescent moon incarnate.

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:11.730
Its feathers are said to have
the power to drive away nightmares.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.280
Cresselia...

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:15.250
She should be
on Full Moon Island...

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.560
Full Moon Island?

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.370
Yeah.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.610
I’ve met her there before.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:22.470
She’s badly hurt...

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:23.280
We need to treat her!

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:27.220
It’s fine, it’s fine!

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:28.870
We’re not enemies.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:43.350
Eevee!

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:51.650
If we face each other earnestly,
people and Pokémon can truly understand one another.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:53.510
It’s fine...

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:56.420
Koharu! Be careful!

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.070
We want to help you.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.610
Let us treat you.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.000
Oh, right, healing herbs.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:24.550
That looks good.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.620
This will sting a bit,
but just try to tough it out.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:31.720
Did someone attack her?

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:34.230
Darkrai... perhaps?

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:35.890
Darkrai?

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:36.730
Yeah.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:40.490
A Pokémon with the power to
give people and Pokémon nightmares.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:44.780
Cresselia can dispel
Darkrai’s nightmares.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.340
In other words...
I guess they’re enemies?

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:49.740
I see...

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:51.250
All right, this’ll do the trick!

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:53.460
You’re amazing, Hikari.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.360
You even know how to make
herbal medicine.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.720
Back when I was traveling
with two friends,

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.410
one of them was a
Pokémon Doctor in the making.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:02.760
He taught me a few things.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.950
Ah, that brings back memories.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:09.310
Now, my other friend... it was like
he never thought about anything but Pokémon.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.630
I guess you could
call him a Pokémon freak?

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:15.060
Oh, I have a friend
who’s just like that, too.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:22.820
So you came to Sinnoh
to watch Contests?

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.690
Not exactly.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:28.630
When I got here, I saw an interview
with a woman named Ayako.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:31.200
Oh, you saw Mom’s interview!

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.540
Mom?

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:36.140
What?! The Ayako I saw on TV
is your mother?

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:36.830
Yeah.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:37.830
Wow!

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:40.100
A legendary
Pokémon Coordinator?!

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.480
Y-Yeah...

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:46.350
I decided I’d chase after
the same goal she did.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:47.880
You did, huh...?

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.660
Koharu, what do
your mom and dad do?

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:52.810
My mother’s an illustrator,

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.910
and my father researches Pokémon.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:57.610
Ooh! He’s a Pokémon Professor?

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:58.750
Yeah.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:04.680
But I don’t like when people assume
I’m going to be a professor just because he is.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:08.610
At one point, I was panicking.
I was trying to think of something I wanted to do.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:14.620
Then I met Eevee,
and realized I don’t need to rush it.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.200
Eevee?

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.380
She’s a bit unique.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:23.010
It’s like she still doesn’t want to decide
what to evolve into.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:26.900
So she copies the moves of other Pokémon,
and tries out all kinds of things.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:27.710
Oh!

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:30.940
So earlier she was copying
Pochama’s move!

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:31.920
Yeah.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:34.750
She seems to really enjoy that.

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:40.690
So I thought that it would be fine for me to hesitate
and just enjoy trying new things, too.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:42.840
Ah, I see.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:47.420
My Pochama decided on his own
not to evolve.

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:48.230
Huh?

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:53.580
He seems to want to stay by my side
as a Pochama forever.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:57.960
At the time, I wasn’t sure
that was really a good idea.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:02.950
But since then,
I’ve gotten a lot closer to Pochama.

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:05.340
So you’ll be fine, just fine!

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.950
Thinking really hard about it
for a long time, then going “Eureka!”...

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:11.920
That’s how the greatest
dreams are born, I bet.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.350
Yeah!

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:17.820
Hey, Koharu...

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.480
You should enter
the Contest after all!

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.770
Huh?
Where’d that come from?

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:24.490
Trying things out
is more fun, right?

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:26.650
Come on!
Let’s practice, let’s practice!

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.410
Pochama!

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.420
Here we go, Koharu!

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:39.940
Right!

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:41.760
Pochama!

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:43.130
Charm up!

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:49.430
Pochama! Whirlpool!

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:00.770
Wow...

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.790
That’s a taste of what it’s like.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:13.030
Wow! That was so beautiful!

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.910
H-Huh? You want to try?

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:22.010
It’ll be fine, it’ll be fine!
You can do it!

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:25.800
Um... Now, then...

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.460
Ch-Charm up!

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.600
Eevee! Whirlpool!

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.460
Wow!

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:43.310
You did it!

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:48.980
Wh-What went wrong...?

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:53.040
It’s fine, Koharu...

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:56.400
It’s not fine...

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:03.670
Does this look good?

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:05.380
Yeah, you’ve got it!

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:08.380
Get well soon, Cresselia.
You hear me?

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:15.480
She’s so pretty.

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:21.560
Cresselia can use a move called Crescent Moon Dance,
which heals up her allies’ wounds.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.780
Crescent Moon Dance, huh?

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:25.960
That must be beautiful.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:37.490
Huh?

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:41.500
Where... am I?

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:43.160
Hikari?

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.710
Eevee?

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:46.220
Pochama!

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:47.590
Where are you?!

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:48.330
Hikari!

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:49.210
Koharu!

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.250
Where are we?

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:53.260
Huh?

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.760
A town?

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.550
What’s going on?

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:03.890
What happened?

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:06.650
They all look like
they’re having bad dreams...

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:12.780
Darkrai!

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:14.100
Then...

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:17.220
Darkrai must be giving
everyone nightmares!

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:22.290
It looks kinda lonely...

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:27.970
Cresselia?!

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:42.930
Everyone’s waking up!

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.360
That’s what Cresselia can do?

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:49.410
Darkrai...

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:58.980
W-Was that a dream?

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:01.070
Huh? Where’s Darkrai?

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:02.880
Huh? You also saw it?

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:05.330
“You also saw it?”...
<i>You</i> saw it?

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.460
A town covered in fog...

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:10.080
Darkrai and Cresselia...

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:13.460
Cresselia!

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:17.820
That’s the same gaze
as in the dream!

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:19.840
What we just saw,
could that have been...

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:22.000
Cresselia’s dream?!

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:25.180
Darkrai’s not around here...

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:27.630
If we had some sort of clue...

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:33.440
It’s an Usohachi!

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.140
Doesn’t it look like
it’s having trouble sleeping?

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:39.420
It could be having
a nightmare...

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:40.450
That means...

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:42.950
Darkrai has to be close!

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:47.860
Darkrai!

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:50.580
No one can sleep
because of your nightmares!

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.080
Go back to
New Moon Island!

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:55.640
What?

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:56.840
Gotta be something that way.

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:58.010
Let’s go!

00:10:58.700 --> 00:11:00.340
Y-Yeah!

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:05.000
She’s flying!

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:10.140
Are you okay, Cresselia?

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:14.430
Darkrai!

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:16.780
So it really <i>was</i> Darkrai who...

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:17.570
No!

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:18.940
You stay away from her!

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:25.310
So? Any luck?

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:27.020
Nope, nothing.

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:27.860
Meow?!

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:28.540
Spot it?

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:31.290
It’s Darkrai, meow!

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.620
Darkrai?

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:37.800
That’s right, the bowl-headed four-eyes
said Sakaki was after Darkrai, too...

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:38.910
Then we should...

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:40.050
...catch it first!

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:42.440
Vending, come on!

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:46.970
Cresselia?

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:49.880
That gaze again...

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:53.240
Are... Are you telling us
not to fight it?

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:56.400
What?

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:58.030
There’s the Darkrai!

00:11:58.030 --> 00:11:59.400
Time to catch it, meow!

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:00.970
Team Rocket!

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:02.640
Wait, you know them, too?

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:03.660
Y-Yeah...

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:06.470
Rocket...

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:07.450
Vending...

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:09.200
Secret!

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:12.080
What’re we gonna get?!

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.800
The Gripper Pokémon,
Yonoir!

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:17.340
The Meteorite Pokémon,
Lunatone!

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:19.220
Yonoir, deal with them!

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.930
Lunatone! Moon Force!

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:30.700
Let’s run while we can!

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:33.030
Yeah. Let’s go, Cresselia.

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:44.540
No way...

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:46.280
What do we do now?

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.200
Someone’s coming!

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.370
Everyone, get ready!

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:54.460
Huh?

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:00.290
Pocket Monsters!

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:10.360
Huh?

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:11.430
How come...?

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:12.130
Hikari!

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:12.980
Satoshi!

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:14.780
I can’t believe it!
It’s been so long!

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:17.440
Wh-Why are you with Koharu?

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.390
What? You know each other?

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:22.190
Huh? You know Satoshi, too?

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:23.910
What a coincidence!

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:26.410
What’re you two doing
all the way out here?

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:27.510
Hold on a second.

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:29.870
Let’s settle down
and go over things.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:34.540
Oh, so you’re friends
that traveled around Sinnoh together.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:37.250
Yeah, together with a guy
called Takeshi.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:40.710
I was surprised to find out
you knew Koharu.

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:43.060
Same to you...

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:45.090
And you had
Cresselia with you!

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:48.050
Hey, when you mentioned
a Pokémon freak...

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:49.750
Yeah, I meant Satoshi!

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:50.970
I knew it!

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:53.360
Why are you here
all by yourself, Koharu?

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:56.090
Uhh... Well,
lots of things happened...

00:13:56.090 --> 00:13:59.810
And you two are here
investigating the nightmares, right?

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:00.480
Yeah.

00:14:00.850 --> 00:14:03.110
We were pursuing Darkrai.

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:04.740
Darkrai?!

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:11.040
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:16.870
I thought we’d fly further...

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:17.930
Yeah, meow...

00:14:17.930 --> 00:14:20.080
I’m not giving up yet!

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:21.410
Huh?!

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:23.460
Darkrai went to Cresselia?

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:25.150
That means...

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:28.520
It was wandering around
because it was looking for her?

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:29.700
But why?

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:32.190
Cresselia was really hurt, right?

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:33.220
In that case...

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:37.850
Basically, Cresselia battled with Darkrai,
took damage, and ran away!

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:39.920
Then Darkrai came after her...

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:40.650
I get it!

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:42.110
Hold on!

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:44.950
I... don’t think that’s right.

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:46.510
I don’t really get it,

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:49.860
but I don’t think
Cresselia and Darkrai are enemies.

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.700
I agree.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:55.480
But you said they nearly
ended up battling, right?

00:14:55.480 --> 00:15:01.120
I wonder... if that was just Darkrai
being mad at us, thinking we’d hurt Cresselia.

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:02.380
But then...

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:03.750
Who did this?

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:07.010
What?

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.870
Cresselia located!

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:10.090
Capture it.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:11.850
Don’t let it get away again!

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:12.850
<i>Ma’am!</i>

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:18.980
Team Rocket!

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:20.940
Obstacles inbound.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.980
So <i>you</i> hurt Cresselia!

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:24.300
You’ll pay!

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:26.110
Eliminate them.

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:27.050
<i>Roger!</i>

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:28.110
<i>Go!</i>

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:34.440
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:37.360
Skutank! Flamethrower!

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.280
Aceburn! Blaze Kick!

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:49.670
Dokurog! Venom Shock!

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:55.800
Pochama! Bubble Beam!

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:59.600
Dosaidon! Stone Edge!

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:05.610
Bunyat! Erratic Scratch!

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:09.030
Eevee! Tackle!

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:18.580
That’s...

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.330
Darkrai!

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:27.540
How lucky
to find Darkrai here, as well.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:29.410
Capture it along with Cresselia!

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:31.300
Skutank! Flamethrower!

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:33.100
Dokurog! Venom Shock!

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:43.090
Darkrai helped Cresselia!

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:45.280
So they weren’t enemies
after all!

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:47.150
Agh... Attack, Skutank!

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:52.150
Good job, Darkrai!

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:53.780
All right!
Everyone, go for it!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:16:59.660
Ugh...

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:00.910
Fire the electroshocker!

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:09.170
Full power!

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:14.680
We gotta help Darkrai!

00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:20.390
Stop making yourselves a nuisance
and stay out of our way.

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:22.370
Now, grab Darkrai!

00:17:32.610 --> 00:17:33.860
What...?

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.200
Darkrai...

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:43.120
Its wounds are fading away...

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.620
Crescent Moon... Dance...

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:47.750
It’s beautiful...

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:55.920
Cresselia!

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:17.260
Im... possible...

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:23.990
Use Iron Tail!

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:27.390
Thanks, Pikachu!

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:29.880
Hold it!

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:31.690
The ones
who’ll get all the glory...

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:33.260
...by catching Darkrai...

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:34.760
...are us, meow!

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:37.400
Promoted... to... admins...

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:38.650
Rising up... the ranks...

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:39.380
Meow...

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:42.930
Huh, those guys were here.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.890
Yeah, they were.

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:46.270
Forget them,
how’s Cresselia?!

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:47.390
Right!

00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:49.140
Cresselia...

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:51.570
She used up all her power...

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:13.860
Her strength is coming back!

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:16.140
That’s... Moonlight!

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:17.800
Oh, because the clouds
went away...

00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:20.970
Darkrai did it
to help Cresselia!

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:35.830
I think they’re going home.

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:38.060
Back to Full Moon Island
and New Moon Island.

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:42.260
So Darkrai was searching
for the wounded Cresselia.

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:45.270
I thought they were enemies...

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:48.580
But maybe they’ve actually
been looking after one another.

00:19:48.990 --> 00:19:51.770
Darkrai gives everyone
nightmares.

00:19:51.770 --> 00:19:58.280
But it can’t control that power,
so it always ends up hated and alone...

00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:04.850
Maybe Cresselia lives on Full Moon Island
because it doesn’t want Darkrai to be lonely...

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:09.680
That’s amazing, Koharu!
You really understand how Pokémon feel!

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:13.930
If we face each other earnestly,
people and Pokémon...

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:16.240
...can truly understand
one another...

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:21.550
Eevee.

00:20:28.550 --> 00:20:29.480
Dad?

00:20:29.480 --> 00:20:30.400
Koharu!

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:32.590
You never called me!
Are you doing okay?!

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:35.550
Are you lonely?!
Having any trouble?!

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:37.640
I’m fine, I’m fine.

00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:39.460
But never mind me.
How was that egg?

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.760
Oh, they all hatched fine.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:45.510
See? They’re all so cute!

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:46.280
“All”?

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:48.890
Hey! Don’t fight!

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:49.950
Okay then, Koharu.

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:52.140
Let me know if you need anything!

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:53.640
Hey, wa— Dad?

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:54.040
Sheesh...

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:54.770
Now you’ve done it, Satoshi!
Sheesh...

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:56.460
Now you’ve done it, Satoshi!

00:20:57.630 --> 00:20:59.760
That feels nice and refreshing!

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:07.370
Hey, if you want to make it to the Contest,
we should leave soon...

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.140
Oh, that’s right.

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:10.290
Pochama, let’s go!

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:13.790
Eevee, we’re leaving!

00:21:17.530 --> 00:21:20.630
She’s more interested in the sea
than the Contest right now, I guess.

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:22.820
Wha...

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:25.510
Oh, well.
It is summer vacation.

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.050
That’s right.

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:29.540
So you should be out here with us!

00:21:29.540 --> 00:21:31.480
Huh? Oh, hold on!

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:39.480
Satoshi, Go, Koharu, and Hikari have experienced
the mysteries and bonds of Pokémon in the Sinnoh region.

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:44.490
Their fun summer vacation is only just
getting started!

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:09.580
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:10.880
Go!

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:15.620
The Pokémon Catching
Adventure Race?

00:23:16.210 --> 00:23:18.620
We’re headed
for the top of that cliff!

00:23:20.950 --> 00:23:23.300
We have a secret plan!

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:24.300
Let’s go!

00:23:24.300 --> 00:23:25.970
Z-Move!

00:23:26.930 --> 00:23:29.090
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:29.090 --> 00:23:32.600
Full Power!
The Alola Deserted Island Race!!
